# Miner Llama v5 preset (in progress): Ornith-1.5-122B, Ornith-1.5-122B Pascal N2P GGUF (valid1: N2P/N3P experts, Q5_0
# output layer) on nine P106-090 cards, 49,152-token context, an 8-bit (Q8_0) attention cache.
# Build: the v5 engine, pascal-p106-v5 at af00bb13b or later (it holds pull request 9's attention kernels; every number
# below for the 8-bit cache was measured on af00bb13b). v4.0's engine does not read the switches below, so this file
# needs the v5 engine; on v4.0 use release/ornith-v4/settings.env.
# This is v4.0's preset (release/ornith-v4/settings.env, explained in release/ornith-v4/README.md) with one switch
# added, GGML_CUDA_MMID_GLU_UNFUSE=2. On the coding-agent check, two runs with it against two without on the same engine
# and rig: every task passed in all four, a decode step 6.3 % shorter (57.22 and 57.70 ms against 61.26 and 61.35 ms at
# the same mix of contexts), a task at equal work 6.6 % shorter (2.04 and 2.05 minutes against 2.17 and 2.21), prompt
# reading the same (docs/data/2026-11-18_r204_ornith_glu_agent/). On the deep lane every reply is the same bytes with
# and without it (docs/data/2026-11-18_c865b_ornith_glu_rig1/).
# Since 2026-11-19 also LLAMA_SERVER_TEXT_REUSE=1, on the owner's word, as in Flint's and Flash-Next's v5 presets: on the
# coding-agent check, two runs with it against two without on rig 2's overclocked boot (docs/data/2026-11-19_r17_ornith_textreuse/),
# no reply read again in either run with it (the plain runs: 5,321 reply tokens on 2 turns in one, none in the other),
# negligible on every measure and slower on none (a task 1.89 and 1.90 minutes at equal work against 1.87 and 1.89).
# Since 2026-11-24 also an 8-bit attention cache (-ctk q8_0 -ctv q8_0) with pull request 9's two attention switches,
# GGML_CUDA_FATTN_TILE_PASCAL_MIN=1 and GGML_CUDA_FATTN_DEC_PASCAL=4, on the owner's word. On the coding-agent check,
# two runs with them against two with the F16 cache, alternated on rig 2's overclocked boot
# (docs/data/2026-11-24_r232b_ornith_q8_agent/): every task passed in all four, a task at equal work 1.84 and 1.84
# minutes against 1.88 and 1.93, generation 20.39 and 20.45 tok/s against 19.42 and 18.80, a decode step at the same
# mix of contexts 48.79 and 48.66 ms against 51.65 and 51.72. The price is prompt reading: the same 19 prompts took
# 184.21 and 184.23 s against 179.86 and 180.09 (2.4 % more). The attention kernels' times at Ornith's shape on one
# P106 are in docs/data/2026-11-24_r232a_ornith_q8_kernels/. Quality is within noise of the F16 cache up to 49,152
# tokens (docs/data/2026-11-23_c976_ornith_q8_cache_kld/; past 8,192 tokens a perplexity rise of a few tenths of a
# percent is not ruled out); the same check at 65,536 and 98,304 tokens is pending. The cache is half the F16 cache's
# size, est. 612 MiB against 1,152 at 49,152 tokens.
# Since 2026-11-26 also pull request 9's third switch, GGML_CUDA_FATTN_TILE_PASCAL_KDP=1, on the owner's word: the
# prompt kernel scores the 8-bit keys in int8 with dp4a. On the coding-agent check, two runs with it against two without,
# alternated on rig 2's overclocked boot (docs/data/2026-11-25_c1102_kdp_agent/): every task passed in all four, a task
# at equal work 1.79 and 1.80 minutes against 1.82 and 1.84, the 21 prompts read in all four runs 185.30 and 186.07 s
# against 191.94 and 192.84, generation unchanged (20.50 and 20.37 tok/s against 20.40 and 20.15). Quality on the quant
# machine (docs/data/2026-11-26_c1103_kdp_quality/): KLD 0.005951 against the preset without it over 12 stretches of
# 8,192 tokens, inside both rounding yardsticks (0.006160 and 0.005794), perplexity +0.06 % (+0.20 % at 49,152 tokens).
# What each line does to the replies: the tag at the start of its comment (docs/reply_effects.md; python3 -I
# scripts/preset_effects.py counts them). Here 2 [lossy] (the 8-bit cache and its int8 key scoring), 1 [input] (text
# reuse), 1 [sampling], 2 [order], 9 [same].
# Use: . settings.env && env $PRESET_ENV llama-server -m "$MODELS/$PRESET_MODEL" $PRESET_ARGS --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8080
PRESET_MODEL=Ornith-1.5-122B-N2P-N3P-valid1-headQ5_0.gguf

PRESET_ENV=
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_KEEPALIVE=decode"  # [same] v3.0's: a one-thread block per card holds the boost clock while a split decodes; 16.3 against 14.9 tok/s (Q1021, Q1045)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_KEEPALIVE_EAGER=1"  # [same] the keep-alive block ends before a kernel's first launch on a card, so the launch does not wait ~1 s for it; a 2,760-token prompt 24,712.63 and 24,744.13 ms against 26,637.95 and 26,065.24 without (C811, C817, Q1417, Q1426; R140, on Flash-Next)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_SERVER_YIELD=2"  # [same] a step's yield to the server's reader thread wakes it only when a read waits, the same replies (C741, Q1310; R122)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_SAMPLING_TOP_K_ROWS=1"  # [same] the card's sampling chain (-bs, top-k 20) runs one top-k over its output rows and reads the logits unpadded, the same tokens (C691, Q1223; R83; the graph fixed by C802, Q1406)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_HOP_STAGED=1"  # [same] each hop between cards through a pinned host ring; the same replies (FN93b); part of the prompt stack (R162, R166)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_GRAPHS_FORCE=1"  # [same] prompt micro-batches captured as CUDA graphs without the two-call warm-up; the same replies (FN93b)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_MMID_GLU_UNFUSE=2"  # [same] the same bytes in every deep-lane reply (C865b); no fused matrix-vector launch on Pascal (upstream's #32239): the fused products of batches of at most 8 tokens, Ornith's gate and up among them, run as plain launches, which a P106 runs faster; a decode step 6.3 % shorter on the agent check, prompts unchanged, the same replies (C865, C865b, R204; Q1559, Q1593)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_SERVER_TEXT_REUSE=1"  # [input] the model reads its own reply tokens instead of the re-tokenized text; the server keeps its cached tokens where a reply sent back spells the same text in other tokens, so it never reads that reply again; on Ornith negligible and slower on nothing (Q260; R17c-R17f)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_FATTN_TILE_PASCAL_MIN=1"  # [order] one- and two-token calls on another kernel; attention calls of one and two query tokens (decode) go to the Pascal kernels instead of llama.cpp's vector kernel; with the Q8_0 cache one layer's one-token call at 8,192 tokens took 780.62 and 780.19 microseconds against 1,455.09 and 1,455.88 on a P106 (Q1703, Q1706; R232a)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_FATTN_DEC_PASCAL=4"  # [order] another kernel for calls of up to 4 tokens; pull request 9's decode kernel for calls of up to 4 query tokens with a Q8_0 cache at head 256: that call 335.23 and 334.99 microseconds, against 619.89 and 619.59 with the F16 cache the preset had before (Q1703, Q1706; R232a)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_FATTN_TILE_PASCAL_KDP=1"  # [lossy] the queries rounded to 8 bits to score the 8-bit keys; pull request 9's int8 key scoring in the prompt kernel (Q8_0 cache, head 256): a 512-token prompt step 39.67 % faster on a P106, a task at equal work 1.9 % shorter on the agent check, quality inside the rounding yardsticks (Q1770, Q1835, Q1836; C1037, C1102, C1103)
PRESET_ENV=${PRESET_ENV# }

# v4.0's line, unchanged (release/ornith-v4/settings.env):
PRESET_ARGS="-ngl 99 -fa on -c 49152 -np 1 -bs --ctx-checkpoints 4 --cache-ram 0 --jinja --reasoning-format deepseek --temp 0.6 --top-p 0.95 --top-k 20 --min-p 0 -b 4096 -ub 512 -ts 6,6,6,6,5,5,5,5,6 -fit off"  # [sampling] the run line: the makers' sampling (temperature 0.6, top-p 0.95, top-k 20, min-p 0); -fa on, -bs and -b 4096 -ub 512 set the arithmetic's order and the draws; nothing else in it touches the numbers
PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS --ctx-checkpoints-vram 4"  # [same] a slot's newest four checkpoints of the Gated DeltaNet state on the cards, not in host memory; the same replies (FN93b)
PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS --ctx-checkpoints-incall"  # [same] checkpoints taken inside a prompt's call instead of cutting the call; the same replies (FN93b)
PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS -ctk q8_0 -ctv q8_0"  # [lossy] the attention cache rounded to 8 bits; the 8-bit attention cache, read by the two switches above: a task at equal work 1.84 and 1.84 minutes against 1.88 and 1.93 with F16, prompts 2.4 % slower, quality within noise (Q1706, Q1707; R232b, C976)

# Opt-in, not in the preset: the micro-batch taper (release/ornith-v4/settings.env explains it). To turn it on:
#   PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS --ubatch-taper short=600:64"
